    LLM: 'Game: Vazhushal. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Vazhushal ('Wipe') is an Indian Rummy from Chennai (Tamil Nadu). 2-6 players. Unique discard LINE (not pile) â€” all discards visible. Can draw multiple consecutive cards from line if deepest card is used immediately in a NEW meld. First meld must include pure sequence. Players can rearrange own melds. Jokers wild.",
    objective: 'Meld all cards into valid combinations (sequences and sets) and go out first by discarding your last card; or when the stock is exhausted, win by having the highest net score (meld value minus hand value).',
    gameplay: "Draw from stock or discard LINE. Deepest card from line must form NEW meld immediately. First meld needs pure sequence. Sets (3-4 same rank) and Runs (3+ sequential same suit). Can rearrange own melds. Can't lay off on opponents. Jokers wild.",
